{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during your stay. You came in today after a liver biopsy and ultrasound, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. The ultrasound showed something about my liver artery being narrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the ultrasound suggested possible narrowing in the main hepatic artery. That’s why we’re keeping you overnight—to give you IV fluids and do a CT scan tomorrow to get a clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:22:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. Is that serious? I feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. You’re not having any pain or nausea, which is good. The narrowing could affect blood flow, so we want to check it carefully with the CT scan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:25:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the biopsy? Was that for my liver enzymes going up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your alkaline phosphatase and transaminases have been slowly rising. The biopsy will help us see if there’s any sign of rejection or other liver issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:27:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had rejection before, years ago. But my last biopsy was normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your history shows that. We’ll follow up on the biopsy results when they come back, but for now, we’re focused on the blood vessel concern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:30:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my other medicines—am I still taking them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most of them, yes. We held your lisinopril today because of the CT scan with contrast. You can restart it the day after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:32:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. I forgot about that. My blood pressure’s usually okay with amlodipine and metoprolol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re continuing those. Your BP has been stable—148 over 85 earlier, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:35:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my insulin? I had a low sugar episode last week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring that. You had a mild low during your stay—treated with juice and crackers. You can keep your current insulin doses at home, but we may adjust the glargine next time if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:37:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I get confused with the doses sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noted that. Elder Affairs has been contacted to help assess your home safety and medication management. They’ll follow up after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:40:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. I live alone, but I usually manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:41:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We just want to make sure you have the support you need. It’s important with all your medications and conditions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2197-12-12 17:42:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CT scan results are back. The good news is there’s no narrowing in your hepatic artery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief! So the ultrasound was wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not exactly. The ultrasound showed delayed blood flow, which can suggest narrowing. But the CT scan, which is more detailed, shows the artery is open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Anything else from the scan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. There’s a small new blood clot in a tiny branch of the portal vein in your liver—segment 6. It’s small, so we’re not starting blood thinners."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A clot? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s small and not blocking major flow. We’ll monitor it with your liver specialist. It may be related to your history of portal vein issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had the balloon dilation a while back. The main narrowing is better, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the scan shows the main portal vein narrowing has improved since your angioplasty. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:26:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discharge you today. You’ll follow up with your transplant team for the biopsy results and to monitor the small clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:28:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other doctors? Eye, bones, stomach?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep seeing them. We recommend restarting calcium and vitamin D for your osteopenia—discuss that with your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t taken those in a while. My appetite’s better since I started mirtazapine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’re continuing mirtazapine for both your depression and appetite. Keep using your latanoprost drops for glaucoma too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do. And Keppra for my seizures—still twice a day?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 500 mg twice daily. No changes there. All your other meds stay the same, including tacrolimus for your transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I can restart lisinopril tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, tomorrow morning. We’ll send all this in your discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:38:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better knowing the artery isn’t blocked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Just keep all your appointments, especially with your liver team. We’ll make sure they get the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2197-12-13 09:41:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2197-12-13 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. You’re feeling well, no pain, no dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2197-12-13 10:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel fine. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2197-12-13 10:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Nurse will go over your discharge papers, and you should be out within the hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2197-12-13 10:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2197-12-13 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your HCV viral load is still high, but you’re not on treatment now. Your transplant team will decide if that needs to change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2197-12-13 11:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. They’ve held off because of my other health issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2197-12-13 11:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll continue monitoring. Take care, and call if you have any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2197-12-13 11:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2197-12-12 17:19:00",
    "admission_end": "2197-12-13 18:51:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 72-year-old woman with a history of liver transplant for HCV cirrhosis, type 2 diabetes, chronic kidney disease, and essential tremor was admitted for IV hydration and a CT angiogram following an ultrasound that suggested hepatic artery stenosis. She was asymptomatic and had undergone a liver biopsy earlier in the day for evaluation of rising liver enzymes. The CT scan ruled out hepatic artery stenosis but revealed a new small thrombosis in a subsegmental branch of the right posterior portal vein, which will be monitored outpatient. Her home medications were continued with lisinopril held for the scan and to be restarted post-discharge. She experienced a mild hypoglycemic episode managed with oral glucose and will continue her insulin regimen. Concerns about medication management and home safety prompted a referral to Elder Affairs. She was discharged home in stable condition with plans to follow up on biopsy results, the portal vein thrombus, and osteopenia management.",
    "problems": [
      "Dehydration",
      "Portal vein thrombosis",
      "Unspecified viral hepatitis C without hepatic coma",
      "Liver replaced by transplant",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of liver",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other disorders of bone and cartilage",
      "Essential and other specified forms of tremor",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Unspecified glaucoma",
      "Need for prophylactic vaccination and inoculation against influenza"
    ]
  }
}
